md throws the html block away, printing only the heading, the new
paragraph and the tail paragraph.

InsertAfterCommand rebuilds the whole document from parsed blocks,
and MarkdownParser.parseNode returns nil for CMARK_NODE_HTML_BLOCK,
so the html never reaches the output. insert-before splices into the
source instead and keeps the same html, which is why the matching
case insert-before-keeps-an-html-block-elsewhere-in-the-document
passes. insert-after should splice too.
